OL,3,GNEWSAMan, 79, admits murdering his wife
OL,4,Aat home
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man has pleaded guilty to the murder
OL,7,Fof his 84-year-old wife at their home
OL,8,Fin West Sussex.
OL,10,FOn the afternoon of 31 May, emergency
OL,11,Fservices attended an address at Langley
OL,12,FGrove in Aldwick after concerns were
OL,13,Fraised for the welfare of Beryl Pyke.
OL,14,FShe was found dead at the property,
OL,15,Fwith significant injuries to her head
OL,16,Fand chest, according to Sussex Police.
OL,18,FHer husband Michael Pyke, 79, who was
OL,19,Farrested at the scene and charged on 2
OL,20,FJune, admitted murder at Lewes Crown
OL,21,FCourt on Monday, police said.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
